{pad:ignore}
<p><code>{pad:branch}</code> ... <code>{/pad:branch}</code> is a condition for the body of a
<a href="?tag/tree">{pad:tree}</a>: its content renders when the current row of the tree has
children, and is skipped when the row is a leaf. Its usual content is the list markup around a
<a href="?tag/recurse">{pad:recurse}</a> - <code>{pad:branch}&lt;ul&gt;{pad:recurse}&lt;/ul&gt;{/pad:branch}</code>
- so a leaf does not get an empty <code>&lt;ul&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</code>.</p>

<p>An <code>&#64;else&#64;</code> part renders for a leaf instead: a different icon, a link where a
folder gets a toggle. The children are read from the field the tree's <code>children=</code>
option names (<code>children</code> by default); a field that is missing or empty means no
children.</p>

<p>The tag takes no parameters. It belongs inside a tree: under the strict syntax check a
<code>{pad:branch}</code> with no <code>{pad:tree}</code> around it, or without its closing tag, is an
error.</p>
{/pad:ignore}
